     If it's slow on a system which isn't already busy, then almost
certainly your working set is too small.  NetHack needs a lot of memory
or it will thrash a lot due to page faulting, wasting CPU cycles on
system overhead instead of executing the actual program.

     Individual users don't have much control over their working sets.
 $ show working_set
will display values for quota and extent.  Access to memory is pretty
essential for decent performance; WSEXTENT controls this on lightly
loaded systems and has very little impact on other users.  A value of
at least 3000 is recommended; larger is even better.  Your'll have to
discuss this with your system manager.



